      <div type="clause" n="25">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 25</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="25" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>XXIII. Gif mon ceorles mennen to nedhæmde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.30"/> geðreatað, mid V<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.31"/> scill. gebete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.1"/> þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.2"/> ceorle; ⁊ LX<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.3"/> scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="25" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="64" ed="#liebermann"/>XXVI. Gif ciorles mennen to nydhæmede<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.12"/> mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.3-2"/> geþreatað, mid V scll' gebete ðam ciorle and LX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="25" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="62" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ceorles m<hi rend="italic">en</hi>nenes nydhemede. Gyf man ceorles mennen to nydhæmede geðreataþ, mid fif scill' gebete ðam ceorle; ⁊ syhtig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.1-3"/> scill' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="25" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="63" ed="#liebermann"/>Si homo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.22"/> (quis) ceorles<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.23"/> mancipium ad uiolentum concubitum comminetur, emendet ipsi ceorlo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_25.lnote.oe.1-2"/> (id est rustico) quinque sol.; et LX sol. wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="74" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ceorles mennenes nydhemede.] Gif mon ceorles mennen to nedhæmde geðreatað, mid V scill. gebete þam ceorle; ⁊ LX scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="29" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="320" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XXIII} Gif mones ceorles mennen to nedhæmde geðreatað, mid V scill gebete þam ceorle; ⁊ LX schill to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_25.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="63" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_25.lnote.de.2"/> jemand eines Gemeinfreien<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_25.lnote.de.3"/> Sklavin zur Nothzucht zwingt, büsse er dem Gemeinfreien mit 5 Schill.; und 60 Schill. zum Strafgeld [dem König].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone forces a common freeman’s slave woman to intercourse, let him pay the common freeman 5 shillings; and 60 shillings as a fine [to the king].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="75" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone rapes the slave of a commoner, he shall pay 5 shillings to the commoner, and a fine of 60 shillings<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Af_25.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="413" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone rapes a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi>’s slave-woman, he is to pay five shillings compensation to the ceorl, and 60 shillings fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="321" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone rapes a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi>’s slave, let him recompense the <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> with 5 shillings, and 60 shillings as fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_10">Abt 10–11</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_14">Abt 14</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_16">Abt 16</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_31">Abt 31</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="281"><label>possibly influenced by</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_82">Abt 82–85</ref> <quote>Other possible effects of Æthelberht's influence are that Alfred had much more to say than Ine about sexual offences (n. 86)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="307"><ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">In H this clause stands after Af 31.1, numbered XXVI.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-meðe <hi rend="italic">So;</hi> nydhæmede <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-meðe So; nydhæmede Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">62</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fif <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fif Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">über</hi> <hi rend="spaced">geselle</hi> <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">above <hi rend="italic">geselle</hi> So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syxtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syxtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">und</hi> de <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y and de on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> homo <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> quis <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only homo Lond; only quis the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">63</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cirlisc <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cirlisc Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">65</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-les <hi rend="italic">T Hk;</hi> cirlo <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-les T Hk; cirlo Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.oe.1-3" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">64</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Umstellung <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> Rb 25</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the transposition <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> Rb 25</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Notzucht 6; Unfreie 11d; Schutz 15a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Notzucht 6; Unfreie 11d; Schutz 15a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_25.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">56</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q behält Agsä. Endung bei</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q keeps the A.-S. ending</seg></note>
